                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="1024-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_c.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Cardioid" title="Cardioid" ></span>Lewitt Audio MTP 540 DM</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Cardioid Dynamic Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The MTP 540 DM is Lewitt&#8217;s flagship dynamic vocal microphone, intended for applications in the studio, on stage, or in the broadcast industry. It has a fixed Cardioid pickup pattern.</p><p>The mic&#8217;s frequency response is nominally flat from 100Hz to 1kHz, with a smooth +5dB presence peak at 3&ndash;4kHz. The high-frequency response drops rapidly above 15kHz.</p><p><a rel="shadowbox" href="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images//mic_extras/lewitt/MTP540DM.jpg"><img src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/mic_extras/lewitt/MTP540DM-sm.jpg" class="thumb shaft" alt="Lewitt Audio MTP 540 DM" width="200" /></a>The dynamic (moving-coil) capsule is elastically shockmounted within the body, to reduce handling noise.</p><p>The mic uses an output transformer.</p><p>Two versions of the microphone are available:</p><ul><li><b>MTP 540 DM</b> - no switch</li><li><b>MTP 540 DMs</b> - Includes on/off switch on mic body</li></ul><p><a rel="shadowbox" href="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images//mic_extras/lewitt/MTP540DMs-kit.jpg"><img src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/mic_extras/lewitt/MTP540DMs-kit-sm.jpg" class="thumb shaft" alt="Lewitt Audio MTP 540 DMs" width="200" /></a>Both versions are packaged identically: the mics ship in a padded cardboard box, with a mic clip (Lewitt p/n MTP 40 MCs) and a leather storage pouch (p/n DTP 40 Lb).</p><p>The 540 DM and DMs are covered by a 5-year warranty.<p>The <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Lewitt/MTP-540-DM">Lewitt Audio MTP 540 DM</a> is also known as: MTP 540 DMS.</p><p>The mic was released in 2010.</p>
